{"ratings":[{"id":"F1","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A listener can act on a merge notification from a transaction that later rolls back, while committed landing events can remain undelivered until an unrelated publication."},{"id":"F2","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"Cancellation during a pending lookup can cause the factory to discard a confirmed merge and leave runs incorrectly marked unmerged until reconciliation."},{"id":"F3","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"Landing through the owner can permanently record the pull request's own review round as superseded rather than merged, leaving an incorrect resolution for operators or the factory to act on."}]}